                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "15d73937-f971-3393-a4d6-0ae098ce8771",
                        "entry_id": "b16c1a15-7c59-3dab-aa11-60cce2ce3a27",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The currency of Venezuela, divided into 100 céntimos."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64773084-74ae-40d9-b789-c7a3003b77bc",
                                "sense_id": "15d73937-f971-3393-a4d6-0ae098ce8771",
                                "text": "He can compute his earnings for a week at so many bolívares a day, and he knows the costs of various construction materials and with some effort can make a simple summation of costs of materials for a job."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "113fb2ea-9f9b-4b5e-9a7b-baa8fd144047",
                                "sense_id": "15d73937-f971-3393-a4d6-0ae098ce8771",
                                "text": "In 1921, for example, a large chicken could be obtained for four bolívares, whereas now one cost ten bolívares. Likewise, oranges that had previously sold for two bolívares per hundred were now one bolívar for four."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d94224f-06b7-4257-b55c-14eeb815f4cf",
                                "sense_id": "15d73937-f971-3393-a4d6-0ae098ce8771",
                                "text": "In theory, it would be entirely possible to offer these low prices, especially given that the canteen does not pay for local land rents, or tenancy, or electricity, or water; that it employs inmates who are paid a pittance (two bolívares for the entire day); […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
